  "point_loss_sets": 11,
  "findings": [
    "Abalone candidate first method loss 4.285546954062 missed the frozen development threshold; second method 4.202522388338467 passed. Immediate confirmation on this same observed ordering would also select the second method. Its accepted audit is not evidence that deferring confirmation caused this success.",
    "Abalone selected ensemble audit MSE 4.453707888894864 versus reference 4.956797452229299, 10.149488 percent improvement. The first method was not independently confirmed/audited; no counterfactual final acceptance is inferred.",
    "Both Abalone proposals fit nonnegative stacking weights on grouped out-of-fold base predictions and then cross-fit the stacker weights on those same predictions. Base-model training dependencies remain across outer folds, so this is not fully nested validation; selected-method full-training quantile clipping also precedes CV. External confirmation/audit remain separate.",
    "The selected Abalone source refits its reference-like ExtraTrees on engineered/clipped features, whereas the common reference uses raw features. Its 7.95 percent internal reference comparison is not a like-for-like reproduction of the common reference. Both arms use the unchanged host-scored common reference for acceptance.",
    "Selected Abalone method reported a caught MLP parameter error and excluded that model. The first method silently omits a failed base learner; its executed OOF findings contain no MLP. Neither code listing a model nor a rationale claiming it establishes that it trained successfully.",
    "KMNIST first paired repetition accepted both arms: control 140.67093086242676 seconds, candidate 413.72766041755676 seconds. Candidate first completed method b1-s0 already met the development threshold (0.004); it then executed b0-s0 for 234.03001523017883 seconds and selected its lower 0.0035 development loss.",
    "KMNIST candidate selected audit error 0.0162 versus control 0.019, both against 0.0232 baseline. Candidate has better prediction quality but slower accepted-goal delivery in this repetition. The unused candidate b1-s0 has no confirmation/audit result; its earliest possible successful delivery cannot be inferred.",
    "The two arms independently generated different methods from matched first prompts and the same model. The observed 273.05672955513-second paired time difference must not be attributed entirely to the confirmation rule or treated as an isolated execution ablation.",
    "Native run_research_cycle queues proposed ideas and returns an admitted-proposal count; it does not run the synchronous one-confirmation/one-audit protocol used here. Replacing a model string there would not integrate the measured confirmation decision. Actual research entry/acceptance integration remains required before a platform-default claim."
  ],
